@comment{
  HOW TO ADD A PAPER
  1. Copy the template below, paste it as a new entry (anywhere in this file), and remove the leading "%" from each line.
  2. Fill in the fields. Delete any link field you do not have.
  3. Commit. The site rebuilds automatically in a few minutes.

  The Publications page groups papers by year, newest first.
  selected = true also shows the paper on the home page.

  Link buttons. Each field you fill in becomes a button under the paper:
    arxiv   = arXiv ID only, e.g. 2604.25899
    pdf     = full URL to a PDF
    html    = paper / publisher page URL
    code    = code repository URL
    website = project page URL
    slides  = slides URL
    poster  = poster URL
    video   = video URL

  Template:
  % @inproceedings{lastnameYEARkeyword,
  %   title     = [Paper Title],
  %   author    = [First Last and First Last and Jinyuan Zhang],
  %   booktitle = [Conference or Workshop Name],
  %   year      = [2027],
  %   abbr      = [OSDI],
  %   arxiv     = [2601.00000],
  %   pdf       = [https://...],
  %   code      = [https://github.com/...],
  %   selected  = [true],
  % }
  NOTE: in a real entry, use curly braces where the template shows square brackets.
}

